UID:1e9bfbd4ea65d414@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261014T170628Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 10/14/2026: Reminder: Maine eCourts in Region
  6 (Lincoln\, Knox\, Sagadahoc and Waldo County) Virtual Presentation Toda
 y at Noon
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nMaine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp
 \n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome\n
 →\nNews & Announcements\nReminder: Maine eCourts in Region 6 (Lincoln\, 
 Knox\, Sagadahoc and Waldo County) Virtual Presentation Today at Noon\nDat
 e:\n10/14/2026\nTo help attorneys and other stakeholders in Region 6 get r
 eady for eFiling\, the Judicial Branch will hold a virtual presentation by
  Zoom today.\nTopic: Maine eCourts in Region 6: Lincoln\, Knox\, Sagadahoc
  and Waldo County\nDate & Time: Wednesday\, October 14\, 2026 at 12:00 p.m
 .\nPlease click the link below to join the webinar:\nhttps://courts-maine-
 gov.zoom.us/j/96415858276\nPasscode: 522889\nThe Zoom presentation will be
  recorded and posted on the Maine eCourts Training & Resources page follow
 ing the live session.\nDistrict and Superior Courts in Lincoln\, Knox\, Sa
 gadahoc\, and Waldo counties (comprising Judicial Region 6) will transitio
 n from paper filing to electronic filing (eFiling) on Monday\, December 7\
 , 2026. This includes all case types in the Lincoln\, Knox\, Sagadahoc and
  Waldo County Unified Criminal Dockets (UCDs) and Superior Courts\; and in
  the Belfast\, Rockland\, West Bath\, and Wiscasset District Courts.\nWho 
 Is Required to eFile?\nAttorneys\, government agencies (except law enforce
 ment agencies)\, and parties who file more than six non-emergency cases in
  a calendar year\, are required to eFile in courts that have implemented M
 aine eCourts. Self-represented parties are not required to eFile and can c
 ontinue to file documents as they always have\, in paper at the courthouse
 \, by mail\, or by email if filing a protection from abuse or harassment c
 ase.\nAbout Maine eCourts\nMaine eCourts is a suite of applications and we
 b-based tools provided by Tyler Technologies' Enterprise Justice Software.
  The system allows for the management of court dockets and hearings\, stor
 age of digital case files\, eFiling\, and online payments.\nFor more infor
 mat\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13363851
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13363851
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
