DTSTAMP:20261013T224217Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Federally Required MaineCare Off-Cycle Provid
 er Revalidation Plan: October 2026 Update
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Federally Required MaineCare Off-Cycle Provider Revalid
 ation Plan: October 2026 Update\nFederally Required MaineCare Off-Cycle Pr
 ovider Revalidation Plan: October 2026 Update\nOct 13\, 2026\nAs\nprevious
 ly communicated\n\, the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) r
 equested all states develop and submit a comprehensive two-year provider r
 evalidation strategy\, with priority given to revalidating high-risk provi
 ders.\nYou can find Maine’s two-year plan and a list of all providers i
 ncluded in the off-cycle revalidation on the Office of MaineCare Services 
 (OMS)\nFederally Required 2026-2028 Off-Cycle Revalidation Plan webpage\n.
  OMS grouped providers into five cohorts and sends notices alerting provid
 ers at least 30 days prior to initiating the revalidation window for their
  assigned cohort. OMS additionally sends a 60-day post-initiation notice\,
  per standard revalidation practices.\nMilestones to note:\nCohorts 1 & 2:
  Individual high-risk providers\, providers without an NPI\, Personal Care
  Agencies\, Home Health Agencies\, Hospice\, and Assisted Living Services 
 providers\nOn July 19\, 2026\, OMS mailed a 30-day notice to impacted prov
 iders in Cohorts 1 and 2 announcing that their revalidation window would o
 pen on August 17\, 2026.\nProviders in Cohorts 1 and 2 who do not submit a
  revalidation case by\nFriday October 16\, 2026\n\, will have claims pend 
 until they submit their revalidation case.\nProviders who miss the October
  16th deadline will have until November 16\, 2026\, to submit their revali
 dation case. Any provider who has not submitted a required revalidation ca
 se by that date will be terminated effective November 17\, 2026.\nYou can 
 find more information about the provider revalidation process on our\nProv
 ider Enrollment and Revalidation webpage\n.\nQuestions?\nFor questions abo
 ut this off-cycle revalidation process\, please email\nKenneth Jamison\,\n
 Provide\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/feder
 ally-required-mainecare-cycle-provider-revalidation-plan-october-2026-upda
 te-2026-10
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/federally-
 required-mainecare-cycle-provider-revalidation-plan-october-2026-update-20
 26-10
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:13f3e985b9c3022e@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261013T224217Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] The MaineCare Third Party Liability (TPL) Exe
 mption Request and Attestation Form is Now Available
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			The MaineCare Third Party Liability (TPL) Exemption Req
 uest and Attestation Form is Now Available\nThe MaineCare Third Party Liab
 ility (TPL) Exemption Request and Attestation Form is Now Available\nOct 1
 3\, 2026\nOn\nAugust 3\, 2026\n\, MaineCare announced claims system update
 s to support proper TPL reimbursement processes in accordance with MaineCa
 re Benefits Manual (MBM)\, Chapter I\, Section 1.07 TPL rules. The\nMaineC
 are TPL Exemption Request and Attestation Form\nis now available for TPL e
 xemption request submission.\nRequesting TPL Exemption\nIn accordance with
  MBM\, Chapter I\, Section 1.07 rules\, MaineCare may assess the validity 
 of extenuating circumstance or service code TPL exemption requests to bill
  MaineCare as the primary payer for services delivered to a member with pr
 imary\, public\, or commercial coverage. Providers wishing to apply for TP
 L exemption to bill MaineCare as the primary payer must complete and submi
 t the\nMaineCare TPL Exemption Request and Attestation Form\nto the\nTPL M
 edicare Code Exempt Request email box\n.\nMaineCare will review completed 
 forms with the supporting documentation and provide a decision letter of a
 pproval or non-approval via email to the requestor. An exemption request a
 pproval letter is valid only for a specific member for a defined duration\
 , no greater than 12 months. The exemption request approval letter must be
  attached to all applicable MaineCare claims for dates of service during t
 he approved time. Claims without a valid and up-to-date approval letter ma
 y result in denials.\nProviders are responsible for maintaining exemption 
 request renewals by submitting a subsequent MaineCare\nTPL Exemption Reque
 st and Attestation Form\nat least 30 calendar days prior to the expiration
  date specified in the approval letter.\nLimited Retroactive TPL Exemption
  Review Period\nFor a limited time\, MaineCare will consider conti\nhttps:
 //www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-third-part
 y-liability-tpl-exemption-request-and-attestation-form-now-available
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-
 third-party-liability-tpl-exemption-request-and-attestation-form-now-avail
 able
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:15df90ca2456269e@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261013T140732Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] System Remittance Advice (RA) and 835 Limitat
 ions
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			System Remittance Advice (RA) and 835 Limitations\nSyst
 em Remittance Advice (RA) and 835 Limitations\nOct 13\, 2026\nAttention Nu
 rsing Homes\, Hospitals\, and Private Non-Medical Institutions\, Appendix 
 C & F (PNMI-C-F): Claims RA/835 Issues\nFollowing the\nMIHMS upgrade\n\, t
 here are open issues affecting some RA/835s.  The issues are high priori
 ty for a fix that is underway\; we are currently targeting to fix the issu
 es by the end of October and will send another communication when the issu
 es have been resolved. This message provides details of the issues and ava
 ilable workarounds until the issues are fixed.\nCost of Care Reporting for
  Nursing Home\, Hospital Claims\, and PNMI-C-F\nNursing Home and Hospital 
 claims for members with cost of care are not being reported with the appro
 priate Claim Adjustment Reason Code (CARC) needed for balance billing memb
 ers.\nPDF RA – CARC 142 is not being reported for cost of care.\n835 –
  CARC 96 is being reported in error.\nAs a workaround until the fix is in 
 place\, MaineCare will provide a report that can be accessed on the\nMaine
 Care Partner Portal\n. On the Dashboard\, navigate to Reports > Other Repo
 rts > “Cost of Care Report.” This report will be available on Mondays 
 for the claims finalized on the prior Wednesday. Because this week’s cla
 ims will be finalized on Thursday\, the first report will be available no 
 later than Tuesday\, October 20\, 2026.\nSpenddown Reporting for Provider 
 Claims\nClaims with spenddown are not being reported with the appropriate 
 CARC needed for balance billing members.\nPDF RA – CARC 142 is not being
  reported for spenddown claims.\n835 – CARC 96 and/or CARC 178 is being 
 reported in error.\nAs a workaround until the fix is in place\, MaineCare 
 will provide a report that can be accessed on the MaineCare Partner Portal
 . On the dashboard\, navigate to Reports > Other Reports > “Spend Down R
 eport.” This\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletin
 s/system-remittance-advice-ra-and-835-limitations-2026-10-13
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/system-rem
 ittance-advice-ra-and-835-limitations-2026-10-13
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
